# ai-tools systemd preset.
#
# The handback privilege-bridge socket is the single root path the ownership handback
# runs over (the per-turn hooks and the session-end sweep both reach ai-tools-chown
# through it). Without it every CHOWN fails and files the agent writes stay
# ai-tools-owned, surfacing later as git "dubious ownership". So it is enabled by
# default: %systemd_post applies this preset on INITIAL install only, which brings the
# socket up on a fresh package install yet leaves a later operator `systemctl disable`
# untouched across upgrades.
#
# Numbered 85 so it is read before the distribution's 90-default.preset (which commonly
# ships `disable *`), giving this enable precedence.
enable ai-tools-handback.socket
